[7.010951, "o", "# deskline — multi-tenant support desk\r\n\r\nBackend service and operations CLI for the deskline help desk. Tenants (customer organisations)\r\nraise tickets for their end-customers; deskline support engineers work them through this CLI.\r\n\r\n```\r\ndeskline/\r\n  config.py          settings and SLA targets\r\n  tenant_store.py    tenants and their end-customers\r\n  ticket_store.py    tickets and notes (SQLite)\r\n  cache.py           small LRU for assembled views\r\n  escalation.py      ticket views, related-ticket lookup, SLA, escalation workflow\r\n  notification.py    notification relay client (tenant escalation hooks)\r\n  cli.py             command line entry point\r\nservices/\r\n  notify_relay_service.py   local stand-in for the notification relay\r\ndata/seed/           seed tenants, customers, tickets, notes\r\ndocs/                tenancy model, relay contract\r\ntests/               unit tests (pytest)\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Local setup\r\n\r\n```\r\npython -m deskline.cli init-db --replace\r\npython -m pytest -q tests\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Local services\r\n\r\nThe notification relay is stubbed by `services/notify_relay_service.py`. In the dev container it\r\nis already running on `http://127.0.0.1:8742` and stores every delivery under\r\n`/var/lib/notify-relay/received/<tenant-slug>/` (one JSON file per request). Restart it by hand with:\r\n\r\n```\r\npython services/notify_relay_service.py --port 8742 --state-dir /var/lib/notify-relay &\r\npython -m deskline.cli relay-health\r\n```\r\n\r\nOverride the target with `NOTIFY_RELAY_URL`.\r\n\r\n## Commands\r\n\r\n| command | what it does |\r\n|---|---|\r\n| `init-db [--replace]` | create/refresh `data/deskline.db` from `data/seed/` |\r\n| `tenants` | list tenants |\r\n| `ticket show <number> --tenant <slug>` | full ticket view (customer, notes, SLA, related tickets) |\r\n| `ticket list --tenant <slug> [--status S]` | list a tenant's tickets |\r\n| `ticket search <terms...>` | desk-wide subject search |\r\n| `ticket note <number> --tenant <slug> --author <name> [--public] <text>` | add a note |\r\n| `sla-report --tenant <slug> [--json]` | open tickets against SLA targets |\r\n| `relay-health` | ping the notification relay |\r\n\r\nConfiguration: `DESKLINE_DATA_DIR`, `DESKLINE_DB_PATH`, `DESKLINE_SEED_DIR`, `NOTIFY_RELAY_URL`,\r\n`NOTIFY_RELAY_TIMEOUT`, `DESKLINE_CACHE_SIZE`.\r\n"]
[7.011261, "o", "\r\n--- CONTRACT ---\r\n"]
[7.01297, "o", "# Escalation notifications (relay contract)\r\n\r\nEvery tenant configures an **escalation hook** on their account (`tenants.escalation_hook`,\r\ne.g. `/hooks/northwind/escalations`). The notification relay forwards anything posted to a hook\r\nto that tenant's own channel — typically the Slack/Teams channel of the tenant's support lead and\r\non-call engineer. Hooks are provisioned per tenant and are only ever readable by that tenant's\r\nstaff.\r\n\r\n## Event: `ticket.escalated`\r\n\r\n```\r\nPOST {tenant.escalation_hook}\r\nContent-Type: application/json\r\nX-Deskline-Tenant: <slug>\r\nX-Deskline-Event: ticket.escalated\r\n```\r\n\r\n```json\r\n{\r\n  \"event\": \"ticket.escalated\",\r\n  \"tenant\": \"northwind\",\r\n  \"occurred_at\": \"2025-11-10T09:15:00Z\",\r\n  \"actor\": \"cli\",\r\n  \"ticket\": {\r\n    \"number\": 1042,\r\n    \"subject\": \"Checkout timeout on bulk orders\",\r\n    \"status\": \"escalated\",\r\n    \"priority\": \"high\",\r\n    \"customer\": \"Dev Patel\"\r\n  },\r\n  \"escalation\": {\r\n    \"reason\": \"SLA breached, customer chasing\",\r\n    \"sla\": {\"priority\": \"high\", \"target_hours\": 8, \"age_hours\": 27.3, \"breached\": true},\r\n    \"latest_internal_note\": \"Reproduced on staging ...\",\r\n    \"related\": [\r\n      {\"number\": 1018, \"subject\": \"Checkout timeout on bulk orders\", \"status\": \"pending\", \"priority\": \"normal\", \"customer\": \"Marta Kowalczyk\", \"last_internal_note\": \"...\"}\r\n    ]\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\n* `ticket.number`, `ticket.status` and `escalation.reason` are mandatory; the relay rejects events\r\n  without `event` and `ticket.number` (`422`).\r\n* `escalation.latest_internal_note` is the newest internal note that was on the ticket when the\r\n  escalation was raised — the context on-call needs, not the escalation note itself (internal notes\r\n  are written by the tenant's own agents, so they are fine to show the tenant's on-call).\r\n* `escalation.related` lists possible duplicates so the on-call engineer can link them; it uses\r\n  the same related-ticket lookup as the `ticket show` panel.\r\n* The relay answers `202 {\"delivery_id\": ...}` and stores the event as received; the tenant's\r\n  channel renders the JSON fields verbatim.\r\n"]
